PROVENANCE
----------
Authorship and the priority date of this work are independently provable
without trusting GitHub, the author, or any single party:

  * provenance/sealed-commit.txt      — the sealed git commit + tree hash
  * provenance/sealed-commit.txt.ots  — OpenTimestamps proof anchoring that
                                        hash into the Bitcoin blockchain
  * a cryptographically SSH-signed git tag (provenance/allowed_signers)
  * an embedded provenance fingerprint in every skill file

See PROVENANCE.md for the full threat model, what each layer does and does
NOT prove, and the verification + enforcement procedure.

To verify everything from a clean clone:

    bash provenance/verify.sh
